tier: sonnet
branch: feat/work-agent-bearings
depends_on:
owns: src/charon/intake.py, src/charon/adapters/acp.py   # + src/charon/api.py PROVISIONAL if the engine Unit/WorkUnit goal field must carry the body
prompt: (authored on activation)
priority: HIGH — part of the AUTONOMOUS-TICKET-RUNNER cluster (operator goal 2026-06-27).
scope: AUTONOMOUS-TICKET-RUNNER (cluster 2/3). The dispatched agent gets FAR too little context to
  autonomously COMPLETE a ticket — it receives only the ticket TITLE as its prompt. VERIFIED ON
  origin/master 2026-06-27:
    - `intake.py` builds each `PlanUnit` with `goal=item.title` (intake.py:536 and :550) and
      DISCARDS the ticket body/description. The body is parsed only to scavenge inline-code
      `owns` paths (`_INLINE_CODE_RE` over `item.body`, intake.py:188) and to gate "too thin"
      items (intake.py:523-527) — its prose is never carried onto the unit.
    - The ACP dispatch sends ONLY the goal: `acp.py:170` frames the prompt as
      `"prompt": [{"type": "text", "text": unit.goal}]` — a single line, the title.
    - Acceptance criteria (`accept`) are run as the post-hoc GATE but are NEVER shown to the agent,
      so the agent cannot aim at the criteria it will be judged against.
  Result: the agent is dispatched essentially blind ("Add X feature") with no description and no
  acceptance criteria — too thin for autonomous completion.
  FIX: carry the ticket BODY/description onto `PlanUnit` (a new field, propagated through the
  engine Unit so it reaches the backend) and have the ACP dispatch prompt include the body PLUS
  the acceptance criteria (the exact checks the unit must satisfy), so the agent has real bearings:
  what to change, why, and how it will be verified. Keep it agent-agnostic (generic prompt text,
  no opencode-specific framing).
  CONSTRAINTS: agent/provider-agnostic; product-clean (no SLOP/fleet/rig leak); stdlib-only
  privileged core; do not leak secrets into the prompt; the acceptance criteria shown to the agent
  must stay the SAME checks the gate runs (no divergence between what the agent is told and what it
  is judged on).
note: PARKED. Part of the AUTONOMOUS-TICKET-RUNNER cluster (operator goal 2026-06-27: run real
  tickets via a non-Claude agent through `charon work`). Closing all three (WORK-GATEWAY-WIRE +
  WORK-AGENT-BEARINGS + WORK-LAND-PR), plus WORK-OBSERVABILITY for watching it, makes it
  trustworthy end-to-end. Without this, even a correctly-routed agent (WORK-GATEWAY-WIRE) is fed a
  one-line title and cannot reliably finish a real ticket. Activate when the autonomous-runner goal
  is prioritized.

